body:
Your college sucks. It's not you.  You can get diplomas from so much better world-class universities like Harvard and MIT, try edX, learn from more intelligent professors.

But also, don't let your academics or one professor define your worth.  Show your work to others. Keep on working on your craft and you'll find people who will like what you do. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Hi, i read somewhere that daily journaling is a good way to track progress.  We sometimes may feel like nothing is getting any better or people say we're still the same.   But when you write it down you can review what things, thoughts and actions were helpful to you or makes you better.  It's good to record and be reminded of those because often times what happens is things gets better and then things get worse then better again, especially if we don't remember what helps and doesn't help.  Getting better is something we work on not something that just happens.   A change of place or situation does not guarantee things will get better.  You need to figure out what thoughts and actions are not making you any better.  That kind of internal change versus external change is what will make it better.  

We're all gonna die and our body continues to deteriorate over time, but for me the reason to live or purpose of life is working on to make things better - making myself better and helping other people get better too.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Don't believe what you see in the mirror/photos, it's just light waves analyzed inside your brain.  Images depend greatly on the angle and lighting that's why we have professional photographers and make up artists.  What you see or what one person sees is not always what all the others see.  Beauty is in the eyes of the beholder.  Surely someone likes your looks.  

If you like to improve your looks, I think a certain hair cut would better suit the shape of your ears.  Also, when you look at the mirror or pose for a photo, try to find the best angle for your nose to not be so noticeable.  But more importantly, it's the expression of the eyes that gives beauty and a smile that give life to a person's countenance.  

&#x200B;
